{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The New Roads Ahead", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "What Did You Do?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 7, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe past experiences in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general aspects of personal information in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general aspects of personal information in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies general aspects of personal information in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies general aspects of personal information in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies general aspects of personal information in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Past Time Expressions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about things that happened before. </br> Many sentences that talk about things that happened in the past use a past time expression to show this.<br>Here is a list of past time expressions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"last&nbsp;(night / week / year&nbsp;&nbsp;) ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"when I was&nbsp;\u2026\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"yesterday&nbsp;(morning&nbsp;/&nbsp;afternoon)&nbsp;\u2026\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"this&nbsp;(morning&nbsp;/&nbsp;afternoon&nbsp;&nbsp;) ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"when you were&nbsp;\u2026\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the day before yesterday&nbsp;\u2026\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"one year ago&nbsp;\u2026\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in 1990&nbsp;\u2026\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"on Sunday&nbsp;\u2026\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Examples: <br><span class=\"italic\"> Yesterday I had my Spanish class.<br>This morning I called the college. <br>The day before yesterday I worked at home.<br>On Sunday I hung out with some friends.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use Wh/Hw questions to request information about past events. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: <br><span class=\"italic\">When did you go to the park? <br> What time was your appointment? <br> How did you injure your leg?<br> Why did she not come to the party?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the negative form of the past to answer questions. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: <br /><span class=\"italic\">I didn't go to the park last night. <br />I didn't have an appointment yesterday.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "College Life", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Here are some words and expressions about college.<br><br>You need <span class=\"strong\">to apply </span> and <span class=\"strong\">to be accepted</span> before you can go to a college.<br><br>To apply to a college, you submit an <span class=\"strong\">application</span>.<br><br>A <span class=\"strong\">deadline</span> is the date you need to do something before, like submit your application.<br><br><span class=\"strong\">Credits</span> are points that a student obtains after they finish a course. In North America, students usually get 3 - 6 credits for a course.<br>  <br><span class=\"strong\">Grades</span> are the evaluation of a student's performance in a course. Grades are often letters with symbols + or - (A+, B-, etc.).<br>  <br>A <span class=\"strong\">GPA</span> (Grade Point Average) is the summary of a student's grades in all courses. In North America, a GPA is measured by a number out of 4. A GPA of 3.2 is very good.<br>  ", "type": "describer"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "credit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "points a student gets after finishing a course", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can take a year off without losing any credits.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use in college.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "GPA", "type": "name"}, {"content": "Grade Point Average -- the average of a student's grades over a period of time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can apply to the program if I have a good GPA.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hung out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "past tense of the verb to hang out", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: On Sunday I hung out with some friends.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to apply", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to ask for permission, such as to enter a program or school ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want to apply to this college. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to submit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give something formally", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When is the deadline to submit my application? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Do an Internet search for colleges in different countries. Use the keyword \u201ccollege\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find 3 colleges in 3 different English-speaking countries.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out what city each college is located in.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out what students learn there. Is it a high school? A university? A training center?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 2-3 sentences about each college.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the information with your class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research 3 colleges in 3 different countries.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I prepare a presentation on 3 colleges.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give a pr